    "translation": "Mymensingh, in present-day Bangladesh. The original ballad is centuries old; Sen’s edition predates modern copyright terms (Sen died 1939). Use original verses; separate modern annotations and recordings. The linked reprint year is not the composition date. The selection is the original-language text; an existing English translation is not required. Passage update (29 October 2026): Fresh English translation by ChatGPT; editorial draft, not a quoted published translation. Original and English contain the same selection. Regional Bengali wording from linked 1958 reprint transcription; footnote numbers omitted. Final line foreshadows calamity. Narrative of lovers’ shared life rather than invocation. নদ্যার চান rendered as Nader Chand. Bengali specialist review recommended.",
